  "summary": "Postwar design language of clean organic lines, molded plywood and plastic, optimistic color and indoor-outdoor living.",
  "description": "Mid-century modern spans Eames plywood, Saarinen tulip chairs, Nelson clocks and Californian case-study houses: streamlined forms made of new materials, honest structure and cheerful upholstery. Scandinavian and Italian variants softened it with wood and wit. The style was revived massively in the 1990s-2000s and is now the default vocabulary of tasteful interiors, its optimism constantly quoted.",
